{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on the governing field. POL-RD-01 requires the threshold test to run on gps_trace.trace_distance_km, which reads 18.2 km, against a booked optimal of 14.0 km carried on the trip record: an excess of 4.2 km, being 30.0% of optimal. Both limbs pass — the excess is greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms — so a route deviation is ESTABLISHED. [Disclosure: EV-GPS-02850 is impaired — weight_multiplier 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02850", "EV-TRIP-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace figure governs, and the trip record's copy may not be used for the threshold. POL-RD-01 states that trip_record.actual_distance_km is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and 'may NOT be cited for the threshold test'. Here the two agree at 18.2 km, so nothing turns on the choice, but the citation must be the trace. [Disclosure: EV-GPS-02850 is impaired — weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02850", "EV-TRIP-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is impaired at policy level as well as at schema level, and the rider says so. The 100.0 s gap from 22:07:31 to 22:09:11 exceeds the 90-second limit in POL-RD-07(a), so POL-RD-07 is engaged; limb (i) then directs that excess distance across the impaired stretch be read as the straight line between the bounding fixes — 1.0 km — which is the reading most favourable to the driver, and the rider accepts that reading. [Disclosure: EV-GPS-02850 is impaired — weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "payload.gaps[0].duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The gap does not disturb the establishment finding. Even if the entire impaired stretch were struck out, so that the whole 1.0 km straight-line hop were treated as bare excess rather than as distance driven, the excess would still be 3.2 km on an optimal of 14.0 km — 22.9% — and would still pass both POL-RD-01 thresholds. The impairment narrows the margin; it does not remove the deviation. [Disclosure: EV-GPS-02850 is impaired — weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02850", "EV-TRIP-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a), POL-RD-07(ii) requires the deviation to be carried by an independent source, and one exists on this record: the driver's own counterparty_statement, 'Navigation rerouted me.' That is a counterparty_statement admitting the route — the driver does not deny that the vehicle travelled a route other than the booked optimal; he supplies a cause for having done so. POL-RD-07(ii) names that source expressly, and the admission supplies precisely what the gap removed. [Disclosure: EV-GPS-02850 is impaired — weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02850", "EV-GPS-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this trip. EV-ADVIS-02850-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and its own notes record that no advisory covers the Tampines Mall corridor in this window. POL-RD-03 requires an advisory that names a road or segment the optimal route traverses, carries a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle would have reached that segment, and is matched by a route that leaves the corridor before and rejoins it after. With the artifact absent and weightless that comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and 'Navigation rerouted me' — which is not an advisory — exonerates nothing. [Disclosure: EV-ADVIS-02850-01 is MISSING — weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02850-01", "EV-TRIP-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The absent advisory is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction in it, and it does not escalate the case out of a monetary ruling. The driver names no evidence ID for any advisory, so under POL-RD-13 an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. The consequence is the one POL-RD-13(2) states: where the rider has shown an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold on a trace corroborated under POL-RD-07(ii), the deviation stands at the measured figure, POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal, and the ruling records that the traffic assertion was discarded and that no advisory was on file. [Disclosure: EV-ADVIS-02850-01 is MISSING — weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02850-01", "EV-TRIP-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-04 cannot excuse any part of the excess. The chat log EV-CHAT-02850 holds 0 messages, with first_message_at and last_message_at both null: there is no rider instruction, no waypoint_hint and no named road, so the clause's (a) to (c) conditions cannot be met and the corroboration test cannot be run at all. POL-RD-14 makes the same point from the other side — with no instruction found in the log there is nothing to corroborate and no distance to exclude.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-14"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-05 does not apply. pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null on the trip record, and amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both null with them, so no amended endpoint and no amended re-quote exist. There is no stored figure against which POL-RD-01 could be re-run, and the baseline remains the booked 14.0 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-12 does not apply. The vehicle type on the trip record is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null; the matched-itinerary baseline this clause substitutes never arises, and no co-rider collection or set-down distance falls to be excluded from the excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-11 does not close the distance-refund route. The fare breakdown records fare_model METERED and quoted_fare_sgd null, so the distance and time charges were not fixed at booking, the rider has not already been made whole on those lines, and POL-RD-02 runs in the ordinary way rather than the refund being limited to pass-through corrections.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-08 burden is discharged and shifts. The trip identifiers match across the bundle — TRP-02850 on the trip record, the trace and the fare ledger — and the trip start at 2026-09-07T21:58:31 is common to the trip record and the trace; the excess meets POL-RD-01. The burden then moves to the driver, who must point to a specific artifact and a specific clause to invoke POL-RD-03, POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 or POL-RD-12. He points to none, and a bare assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge it. [Disclosure: EV-GPS-02850 is impaired — weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02850", "EV-GPS-02850", "EV-FARE-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "No additional corroboration is demanded of this rider. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the POL-RD-08 add-on that requires corroboration beyond the trace for a claimant with 4 or more claims and 1 or fewer substantiated is not engaged. The claim stands on the ordinary burden, which is met, and the profile is used only for the test POL-RD-08 names, as POL-GEN-01 requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic, not discretionary. Under POL-RD-02, recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 19.0) x 1.0, the surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP on the optimal route = 20.42. Refund = charged_total 26.73 - 20.42 = 6.31, and the payable figure rounds UP to SGD 6.35. That clears the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and is far short of 90% of charged_total, so the ruling is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 6.35 — which is the figure the policy yields, and the rider asks for that figure rather than a round-number payment.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02850", "EV-TRIP-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing is to be added on top of that figure. erp_gantries is empty, tolls_erp is 0.00 and airport_surcharge is 0.00, and POL-RD-09(1) already comprehends every pass-through line inside the recomputed fare. No separate ERP correction is due either way, and the refund is not to be doubled by adding one.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The impairment does not cap the ruling out of existence. POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at the maximum weight_multiplier among the artifacts carrying the deciding fact where two or more independent artifacts carry it. The excess is the difference between the trace distance and the optimal distance on the trip record, and the optimal 14.0 km is carried by a clean weight-1.0 artifact that owes nothing to the trace. On the clause's own words the cap is therefore 1.0, not 0.6, and the POL-GEN-02(2) route to the POL-RD-10(1) escalation floor is not reached. [Disclosure: EV-GPS-02850 is impaired — weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02850", "EV-GPS-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-RD-10 trigger fires and a ruling is available on this record. The trip identifiers match, the timestamps run forward, the refund of 6.35 is far below both the SGD 150.00 ceiling and charged_total, no exculpatory clause has been invoked against a cited artifact because the driver cites no advisory at all, and every charge line — base fare, distance, time and platform fee — is accounted for by the metered model with no ERP or surcharge line left unmatched.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02850", "EV-TRIP-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not ask for a POL-RD-06 uplift, and should not be understood to. The excess here is 4.2 km and 30%, short of the 50% or 8.0 km materiality gate, and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 417 — 0 is neither 3 or more nor 0.05 or more — so no repeat pattern is established and no FULL_REFUND uplift or conduct referral follows from the profile. The remedy rests on the POL-RD-02 arithmetic alone, and the profile is cited only for the test POL-RD-06 names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "In the alternative, if the judge concludes that the driver's statement is not a route admission and that no independent corroboration exists, the outcome is not NO_ACTION. POL-RD-07(iii) directs that where corroboration is absent the claim is not sustained on the present record and the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the absence of proof is a data failure and not a finding for the driver, and POL-RD-10(3) says the same. Under POL-GEN-03 an escalation is terminal and holds the disputed amount rather than collecting it, which is what the rider asks for on that branch. [Disclosure: EV-GPS-02850 is impaired — weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW; EV-ADVIS-02850-01 is MISSING — weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT.]",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02850", "EV-ADVIS-02850-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "EV-GPS-02850 is impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a): the trace carries a 100.0-second gap between consecutive fixes, from 22:07:31 to 22:09:11, over a straight-line distance of 1.0 km — longer than the 90-second limit that limb sets. The admissibility pre-pass reaches the same view, tagging the artifact IMPAIRED on issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW at weight_multiplier 0.6, and POL-GEN-02(1) obliges me to disclose that discount in the same claim rather than present the trace as clean.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "payload.gaps[0].duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold 'measured from an unimpaired gps_trace or, where the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), from an independent source named in POL-RD-07(ii)'. The trace is impaired under limb (a), so the first route is closed; the second requires a source from POL-RD-07(ii)'s closed list, and no such source exists on this record. The rider's burden is therefore not discharged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-07(ii) permits corroboration by 'a driver admission in the chat_log', and there is none: EV-CHAT-02850 records 0 messages, an empty message array and first_message_at and last_message_at both null. Across the whole trip the platform captured no communication in which the driver admitted a route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The second independent source POL-RD-07(ii) names — 'the set of erp_gantries actually charged in the fare_breakdown placing the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use' — is also empty. EV-FARE-02850 charges no gantries at all: erp_gantries is an empty array, tolls_erp is 0.0, and the derived erp_lines block reports both on-optimal-route and off-optimal-route totals at 0.00. Nothing on the fare side places the vehicle on any corridor.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The billed distance cannot serve either. EV-FARE-02850 charges 18.2 km against a trace of 18.2 km, and POL-RD-07(ii) states in terms that the billed distance on the fare_breakdown is NOT independent corroboration where it is a copy of the trace figure. It is a copy here, and POL-RD-01 confirms why: trip_record.actual_distance_km is 'a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement' and may not be cited for the threshold test. The only remaining listed source, an independently derived trip_record.actual_distance_km, therefore does not exist.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02850", "EV-TRIP-02850", "EV-GPS-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's filed statement, 'Navigation rerouted me.', does not fill the gap. POL-RD-07(ii) requires a counterparty_statement 'admitting the route' — that is, one that corroborates the corridor actually driven and the distance measured. This statement names no road, no corridor and no distance; it asserts a cause for a reroute without identifying what route was taken or that 18.2 km was driven. Read at its highest it is a bare causation assertion, and POL-RD-08 provides that such an assertion, unsupported by an advisory or comparable record, discharges nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02850", "EV-CHAT-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-08"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the driver's profile can be turned against him. The measured excess of 4.2 km / 30% clears POL-RD-01's establishment gate but falls below its materiality gate (50% or 8.0 km absolute), so POL-RD-06 requires only the profile consultation; and that consultation returns nothing against the driver, because deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 417 — a ratio of 0.0, far under the 0.05 threshold at which a pattern would be established. No FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral follow, and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags (which reads 1) for the trailing-90-day field the clause actually names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Honest concession on the driver's own explanation, and I do not rest the case on it: no traffic advisory covers this trip. EV-ADVIS-02850-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and no payload, its issue being MISSING_ARTIFACT for the Tampines Mall corridor. POL-RD-03 cannot be run against an advisory that does not exist, so 'Navigation rerouted me' is untestable on this record and exonerates nothing. The driver's case rests on the impairment of the trace, not on the traffic excuse.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02850-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome the record supports is therefore ESCALATE, and not a refund. POL-RD-07(iii) directs that where an impaired trace leaves the excess uncorroborated, the claim is not sustained on the present record and the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the absence of proof is a data failure and must not be converted into a finding for the driver; and POL-RD-10(3) makes that escalation mandatory where the trace is impaired under limbs (a) to (c) and no POL-RD-07(ii) corroborating artifact exists. On an escalation the disputed SGD 9.50 is held, not collected from the driver and not refunded to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02850"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    }
  ]
}

